  "notes": "{凭|もた}れる has two distinct meanings: the physical action of leaning and the sensation of stomach heaviness.\n\nWRITING:\nThe kanji {凭|もた} is rarely used in modern writing; this word is often written in hiragana as もたれる.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{胃|い}→胃：01706_i⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧もたれる: to sit heavily on the stomach\n- ⟦{背|せ}もたれ→背もたれ：17768_semotare⟧: backrest (of a chair)",
